## 5.2. Can indicators and metrics replace peer review?

A common refrain during the process of collecting evidence for this review has been the warning to avoid tensioning an idealised problem-free notion of peer review against an overly simplistic and negative construction of metrics. The picture is clearly far more complex than this, and once again it is crucial to emphasise the role that context must play when making decisions about research assessment processes and strategy.

