# 10.2. Recommendations

This review has identified a number of specific recommendations for further work and action on the part of key actors in the UK research system. These draw on the evidence we have gathered, and should be seen as part of broader attempts to strengthen research governance, management and assessment which have been gathering momentum, and where the UK is well positioned to play a leading role internationally. We have grouped the recommendations under a number of thematic headings, as follows:

- Supporting the effective leadership, governance and management of research cultures;
- Improving the data infrastructure that supports research information management79;
- Increasing the usefulness of existing data and information sources;
Using metrics in the next REF;
- Coordinating activity and building evidence.
